                <pb facs="0613" n="541" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg541"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 22160.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                    King.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-11-04"><hi rendition="#italic">November 4,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Wilson informs Mr. King that the department considers that it would not be
                    advisable, in view of his diplomatic privileges and immunities, for him to act
                    as executor under will as reported in his telegram of the first instant.</p>
            </div>
